C Language
A compiled, low-level programming language that lets you write fast, precise instructions to control memory and hardware directly.

Arduino uses C++ (C++ is C plus extra features)
Raspberry PI uses C and Python (C is simple, low-level, procedural)

C-Basics:
- variables
- if/else
- loops
- functions
- reading/writing pins
- serial printing
- analog vs digital signals
- timing and delays